{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>And his spirit was troubled.</b> וּמִטַּרְפָּא רוּחֵיהּ — his spirit knocked within him like a clapper; and regarding Nebuchadnezzar it says, ״וַתִּתְפָּעֶם רוּחוֹ״ (Daniel 2), because there were two strikings there — forgetfulness of the dream and concealment of its solution (Bereshit Rabbah)." "<b>Magicians.</b> Those who pick through the bones of the dead, who divine by bones. טִימֵי is 'bones' in Aramaic; and in the Mishnah, ״בַּיִת שֶׁהוּא מָלֵא טִימַיָּא״ (Oholot 17) — full of bones." "<b>And there was none who interpreted them to Pharaoh.</b> They did interpret them, but not to Pharaoh — their voice would not enter his ears, and he found no satisfaction in their solution, for they would say, 'Seven daughters you will beget and seven daughters you will bury' (Bereshit Rabbah)."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 41, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:02:56.139939132Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}